# 4. How do we check whether a Queen's position is safe?

This is the most important concept in your assignment.

Before placing a Queen, we must check three conditions.

### Condition 1: Same Column

Check whether another Queen already exists in the same column.

Example:

```text
Q  .  .
.  .  .
Q  .  .
```

Both Queens are in Column 1.

This is an invalid arrangement.

### Condition 2: Left Diagonal

Check whether another Queen exists on the upper-left diagonal.

### Condition 3: Right Diagonal

Check whether another Queen exists on the upper-right diagonal.

If any of these conditions is true, the position is unsafe.

**Important:** We place only one Queen per row, so we don't need to check the same row separately.

