# 6. Complexity Analysis

Your uploaded manual does not provide a detailed complexity analysis, but these are the standard complexities of the N-Queens backtracking algorithm.

### Time Complexity

\[
\boxed{O(N!)}
\]

**Why?**

- For the first row, we have N possible positions.
- For the second row, at most N−1 remaining columns.
- For the third row, at most N−2 remaining columns.
- This continues until all rows are explored.

Therefore, the worst-case search space is bounded by:

\[
N \times (N-1) \times (N-2) \times \cdots \times 1
\]

\[
= N!
\]

The actual number of explored positions can be smaller because unsafe positions are rejected early.

### Space Complexity

\[
\boxed{O(N^2)}
\]

When we use an N × N matrix to represent the chessboard.

The recursion stack requires O(N) additional space.

### Complexity Summary

| Parameter | Complexity |
|---|---|
| Time Complexity | O(N!) |
| Chessboard Space | O(N²) |
| Recursion Stack | O(N) |
| Total Auxiliary Space | O(N²) |

